Just the other day, I had a wonderful inspiration that might keep
us all from charging that rothe only to find out its a mumakil.

Why don't we use the letter Q for Large Quadrupeds, in addition
to the q for Small Quadrupeds.  After all, we already have this
for humanoids (h and H).  I think that I'd definitely notice the
difference when this big Q starts lumbering across the screen.

Yes, right now, Q is being used for Quantum Mechanic.  I wonder
whether we couldn't just throw them into the @'s, along with
the elves and the nurses and the shopkeepers.  I imagine that
some of you physicist Nethackers occasionally like to think
you're human.

Of course, I suppose the drawback with this is that some character
classes might have a harder time getting Intrinsic Speed.
I personally have never eaten a quantum mechanic in order to
speed up.  Do lots of people do this?

If so, I suppose it might be possible to turn off the
intrinsic aggravate if what you eat happens to be a quantum mechanic.
On the other hand, maybe the 'you are what you eat' philosophy
should give you intrinsic speed from ants, bats, bees,
centaurs, cobras, leocrotta, unicorns, xans, etc.
(i.e. the really fast monsters).

I suppose if this really sounds too abusive, one could always
slow down be eating certain very Slow critters (like the brown
pudding).

Comments?  Flames?  Protests?  Dev Team?

